    description: "FOUND 2026-10-03 by WI-dibit while sweeping \"factories/classes returning a sending object\" in the python stdlib. SAFE DIRECTION (inconclusive, recall loss), listed so the family is enumerated rather than implied closed.\n\nObserved on real verify-claims output, host_secret -> network claim, the secret passed straight into the send; each reads `inconclusive` with \"could not classify (<module>)\":\n- urllib.request.URLopener().open(url, secret)  -> could not classify urllib.request.URLopener (also FancyURLopener; open/retrieve/open_http/... send; deprecated, present 3.10-3.13)\n- smtplib.SMTP_SSL(host).sendmail(..., secret)  -> smtplib, smtplib.SMTP_SSL (the SMTP rows are keyed to the exact class smtplib.SMTP; SMTP_SSL / LMTP inherit the methods but not the slot)\n- smtplib.SMTP(host).login(user, secret)        -> smtplib, smtplib.SMTP (login / starttls / ehlo / docmd / send are unrowed; the constructor connects when given a host)\n- ftplib.FTP_TLS(host).storbinary(...)          -> inconclusive (FTP_TLS slot unrowed; FTP's rows are exact-class)\n- imaplib.IMAP4_SSL(host).login(user, secret)   -> imaplib, imaplib.IMAP4_SSL (no imaplib rows at all)\n- poplib.POP3_SSL(host).pass_(secret)           -> inconclusive (no poplib rows)\n- multiprocessing.connection.Client(addr).send(secret) -> inconclusive (Client is a FUNCTION returning a Connection; the PascalCase rule types it as the function's own name)\n- ssl.SSLContext.wrap_socket(sock).sendall(secret) -> inconclusive (member return SSLSocket not propagated; WI-kozaj's residual)\nNot checked: nntplib, telnetlib, xmlrpc.client.ServerProxy method forms, asyncio.open_connection tuple unpacking. Each class needs its own surface read (CPython source) -- a mechanical copy of the parent's rows is the mistake (LIVE rule 3); subclass-slot inheritance of rows may be the structural answer and should be checked first."  # f208
    fields: {}  # f208
- op: discuss  # 1fc0
  at: '2026-10-05T04:52:29Z'  # 1fc0
  by: agent  # 1fc0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1fc0
  clock: 2  # 1fc0
  nonce: 1fc0  # 1fc0
  message: "FROM WI-tumol (branch jgstern-agent/fix/tumol, commit 206e733d13, not merged): py.py now types a MEMBER call on a typed receiver from its library_signatures row (_member_return_type), not only when the row preserves the type, and types a `with` item derived from a typed receiver the same way. So two of this item's shapes become one-row fixes once each class's surface is read: `ssl.SSLContext.wrap_socket: ssl.SSLSocket` (the \"member return SSLSocket not propagated\" line), and `multiprocessing.connection.Client: multiprocessing.connection.Connection` (a FUNCTION producer, WI-kozaj's existing mechanism). Not added on WI-tumol: each needs its own surface adjudication and A/B. Also: WI-tumol typed `http.client.HTTPConnection.getresponse` / `HTTPSConnection.getresponse` -> http.client.HTTPResponse, but getresponse itself is still unrowed and HTTPConnection has no completeness entry, so a clean http.client program still reads inconclusive (\"could not classify http.client.HTTPSConnection\") -- same family as this item."  # 1fc0
